{
	"$comment": "Changed file → UI journeys it needs (select.mjs). Paths are repo-relative globs (** any depth, * within a name). A file matching an 'all' rule runs every journey; otherwise the union of every matching rule. Tests (*.test.ts) never select anything. On a pull request (select.mjs --ci) a changed non-test file under 'unmapped_runs_all' that no rule covers also runs every journey; a local selection does not. There, an edit to this file is judged against the base's copy: the other changed files run what either copy names, so an edit can add journeys to the run but never drop one. Keep this in step when adding a journey: every journey must be reachable from some rule (select.mjs --check).",
